  "also": [],
  "brief": "Rosti Group is acquiring Alvi Group to expand its manufacturing platform, while Mitsui Chemicals is acquiring JSR in a $11.6 billion deal to bolster Japan's chip industry.\n\nRosti Group / Alvi Group (Announced): Rosti Group Acquires Alvi Group. Rosti Group is acquiring Alvi Group to expand its manufacturing platform [1, 2]. The deal is expected to increase Rosti Group's annual revenue to €450 million [1]. Rosti Group is expanding its global injection molding operations with the acquisition [2].\nMitsui Chemicals / JSR (Announced): Mitsui Chemicals to Acquire JSR. Mitsui Chemicals is acquiring JSR in a $11.6 billion deal [3, 4]. The deal is being backed by the Development Bank of Japan [4]. The acquisition is aimed at bolstering Japan's chip industry [3].\nArgenx / Unnatural Products (Announced): Argenx Buys Unnatural Products. Argenx is buying Unnatural Products for up to $1.15 billion [5, 6, 7]. The deal was announced and no further details are available [5, 6, 7].\nStrathcona / Greenfire (Announced): Strathcona to Acquire Greenfire. Strathcona is acquiring Greenfire in a $2.1-billion oil sands deal [8, 9, 10]. The deal was announced by Strathcona [8].\nKOBELCO / CNH's Case, New Holland Construction Equipment Business (Announced): KOBELCO to Acquire CNH's Construction Equipment Business. KOBELCO is acquiring CNH's construction equipment business, including Case and New Holland Construction Equipment [11, 12]. The deal was announced by CNH and KOBELCO [11, 12].\nShield / Echodyne (Announced): Shield to acquire Echodyne. Shield is acquiring Echodyne, a radar tech company, in a $5.3 billion deal [16, 17, 18]. The deal is backed by Blackstone financing and will raise $2.5 billion for Shield [13, 14]. The acquisition will double down on Shield's presence in the Seattle area [17]. The deal has been announced [15].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Rumored): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is in talks to buy Momentum Midstream for $5.5 billion [19, 20]. The deal is rumored to be in the works [19].\nXylem / Cornell Pump and Roper Pump (Completed): Xylem Acquires Cornell Pump and Roper Pump. Xylem has acquired Cornell Pump and Roper Pump [21]. The deal is completed [21]. No further information is available [22, 23].",
